<title>USA: Noodle Kidoodle to cut staff, take charge.</title>
<headline>Noodle Kidoodle to cut staff, take charge.</headline>
<dateline>FARMINGDALE, N.Y. 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Noodle Kidoole Inc said it will cut about 20 percent of its administrative staff and limit the number of new store openings in 1997.</p>
<p>As a result of the elimination of staff positions, the company said it will take a $250,000 charge in the fourth quarter.</p>
<p>Noodle Kidoole said it had revenues of $28.7 million for the fourth quarter ended February 1, compared with $16.7 million in the year-earlier period.</p>
<p>The company is a retailer of specialty children's products.</p>
</text>
